 {:seon.task/name "the-slow-test-tail-is-cut-at-its-causes"
  :seon.task/plan "Measured 2026-11-14 [M, tests-3, lands of that day]: a land takes 12-19 min, 4 shards of 150-250 s each; the median test is 171 ms and the mean 1.58 s, and tests of 1 s or more carry 91% of the wall; the 115 tests that share a shard's test root carry 59% of it (0.2-0.6 M ticks each). Target (docs/cost.md, the owner: within 2x is met): a typical change about 1.3 s, a pin change about 25 s. The classes, each cut at its cause, never by a waiver or a cap raised: (1) a test that boots or drives a root where an in-process call proves the same thing: seon.agent-test/root-reads-the-health-the-render-proc-keeps (541 s) goes, covered by seon.problems-test/health-moved-is-health, seon.render-test/the-problems-tile-follows-main-without-reading-it-whole and the-banner-counts-what-root-counts (its docs/health.md cite moves to them); a-task-at-its-cap-is-recorded-cap-never-waiting (189 s) is rewritten on work-with, red under >= made > in the cap check of src/seon/turn.clj; an-agent-whose-store-lacks-a-cited-section, a-root-with-no-provider, a-reply-is-recorded-before-its-evals-run and a-broken-parser-reaches-the-model are rewritten in-process or go as duplicates (a-failed-call-keeps-what-it-sent), each red under a mutation first. Before any of these: is the root tail one render bug (root and deps' test root at ~99% CPU in :render's first pass [M, root])? Sample the test root's CPU against wall on the three slowest; CPU near wall is web's, a wait is ours. (2) a fixture built per test: the wiki is read once (ts/wiki in test_store, read by doc_test and repl_test), loading docs/ only. (3) cost proofs at sizes past what a curve needs: ctx_test's [100 300 1000 3000] go to [100 300 1000] (seon.cost min-points 3). (4) whole-program readers with the filter outside the query: main_test's an-error-names-its-raiser-by-its-var, a-tasks-outcomes-are-read-once and a-key-read-at-load-says-so push it into the datalog, as git-is-read-through-fx does. (5) seon.ctx-test/an-agent-pulled-by-its-implied-joins-validates (5.4 G ticks): malli compiles the derived ref schema again on every path; the validator is compiled once a schema digest (context's or data's code: agreed with them first). Deletes, root-approved only: seon.reader/definition-head and its test, seon.profile/stats-sum (accrue's assertions kept). Proofs are named as each class lands, each with its measured ticks beside its estimate."
