 {:seon.task/name "a-test-that-dies-fails-only-itself"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by context, 2026-11-15 [M root result/c81de8be, result/d0dc1326]: round 3's agent e42f (seon.program/loading-a-changed-file-keeps-its-other-vars-bound) had its fix and proof on its branch, green when run directly, but its proof's batch answered :seon.prove/no-verdict (\"...'s batch answered no verdict for it\"): seon.prove/batch-ended's last case, the batch's run answered but its :reports never named the proof, while a sibling in the batch, seon.agent-test/a-pull-after-its-own-merge-starts-from-what-it-merged, died. The same class held ef96640d earlier the same day. PRIOR WORK: run-children! (seon.agent) already says a child that dies loses the test it ran and the rest of its shard runs in a new child; seon.proofs/run-tests! answers an unloaded test as its own :error (runtime's class for a namespace's load error). So the cause is a gap in that one path, found by rerunning the real batch red first on the agent's branch (:main/task-seon-program-loading-a-changed-file-keeps-its-other-vars-bound, held): which test the death took, and why the proof was never run again. Fix in run-children!/the fold: every granted item ends with its own result, a death the dead test's own :error, never a batch-wide no-verdict. Also: batch-ended's error carries {:test :digest :reported}, but the agent's stored :seon.agent/test-error keeps only type, operation and message: the writer that drops the data is found and fixed in the same change. COST: none on a batch that does not die; one more child for the rest of a shard after a death (~1 fork). Root ranks it next after landing 12. PRIOR WORK [read, src/seon/agent.clj]: seon.agent/child-ended (1438) folds a dead child's run (test-run-answer, 1178: a death is one :error report on the test the child was running, its :running var) and forks the rest of the shard to a new child only when (and (seq rest-todo) (seq died) (or (seq (:ended acc)) (some :var died))) (1454): a death that names no running test, with no test ended in that child, marks the shard done, and its remaining tests are never reported; seon.prove/batch-ended then answers each of them :seon.prove/no-verdict (its :else). HYPOTHESIS [H], to be seen red first on the real batch once agents start again: the sibling's death left :running unset (it died outside a test's started/ended pair, or before its started line was read). PLAN: (1) red first: a unit proof of child-ended over a shard of two tests whose child dies with no :running and nothing ended answers both tests no verdict today; (2) fix at the rule: such a death reruns the rest in a new child once; a second death with no progress answers each remaining test its own :error naming the death and marked unreported (verdict-tx writes nothing for it, so no red is cached against an innocent test), so every granted item ends with its own result and the loop ends in at most two forks; (3) the dropped error data: find the writer of :seon.agent/test-error that keeps only type, operation and message. COST: nothing on a batch with no death; one fork (~65 ms) per death with no progress, at most two per shard. Flow reviews the fold change (it is a proc's state)."
