 {:seon.task/name "a-named-ask-on-main-waits-on-mains-run-never-refused"
  :seon.task/plan "STATUS 2026-11-16: the hold landed (7f4e842206) and the runner sweep (0b667d45c0); LEFT only (a) the JOIN at the same digest, proof seon.prove-test/a-named-ask-main-did-not-select-runs-after-it, and the asker-gone signal (seon.prove/an-asker-that-stops-waiting-tells-its-owner). Found by data, 2026-11-16 [M result/bbd0ab17]: while main's own run holds :main/tests, a judge's named :judge ask on main (seon.reconcile/ask-main) answers :seon.system/refused, so every pilot judged during a main run reads its reds :unknown (run 11's 'stray' reds came from the same refusal, read before the :unknown path existed). CAUSE [M, prove.clj request]: main's commit-notice run (slot [:main nil :main]) and the named ask (slot [:main names :judge]) are different slots; each takes request's last branch, which spawns its own prove agent on the tests branch, and the second spawn is refused by seon.system/spawn! (branch held by a live agent, system.clj:558); finish answers its waiter the refusal. PRIOR WORK, searched (seon.prove: request, run-key/slot, :runs/:waiters, finish, superseding; the :prove service's queue): a run of the same key is joined (:waiters); a run of the same slot at another digest is superseded; items dedup by [test digest] across runs (ask-items, :items with :waiters); none waits for another slot's runner. PLAN, in the proc's own state, no proc, timer or poll (flow's criteria 1-5): (a) JOIN: a named main ask whose names main's in-flight run selects (its plan's :selected, held on the run once planned) becomes a waiter of that run; its answer is the run's, which main-answer reads per asked test. (b) QUEUE: otherwise, or before main's run is planned, the request is held under :held-main [m ...] and re-entered through request when main's run finishes (finish, once, each held request), so it spawns on the free branch. (c) Death and stop: main's run dying, or an item error, answers its waiters through finish as today (a typed error naming the run and its agent) and then re-enters the held ones, which spawn their own run; root's stop answers no-agent; :seon.config.proofs/gate-ms stays only the outside guard. A newer main run superseding the held-for run carries the held list (they re-enter at its finish). PROOFS, red first, in seon.prove-test: a named ask during main's run is answered with main's verdicts, never refused; one whose names main's run did not select runs after it; main's run dying answers its waiters the typed death and the held ask still runs. COST: O(held + waiters) at a finish, one vector in state; no spawn while the branch is held. MEASURED: today the ask costs one refused spawn and an :unknown judge (result/bbd0ab17). FLOW REVIEW 2026-11-16 02:0x, approved with four changes, applied: (1) join only at the same digest (and the run's :selected covering the names), else hold; (2) the hold is on the tests branch's runner: request holds any agentless main ask while any prove agent of the tests branch is in flight, whatever its slot, and each finish re-enters the held asks in order through that same rule (one spawns, the rest stay held); (3) a held ask whose askers are all gone leaves :held-main at re-entry, so no run starts for nobody; (4) the proofs are named, among them two-asks-held-on-the-tests-branch-are-both-answered. BUILT (tests, 2026-11-16 02:0x): the hold on the tests branch's runner (tests-branch-busy?, :held-main, re-enter-held at each kill answered and at a spawn that died), with a runner sweep (runner-done ends every runner whose run is gone and holds no item, which closed a leak: a runner holding an item at its run's end was never killed); proved by two-asks-held-on-the-tests-branch-are-both-answered, a-named-ask-during-mains-run-is-answered-with-its-verdicts and a-dying-main-run-answers-its-waiters-and-the-held-ask-runs. LEFT: (a) JOIN at the same digest, an optimization of the hold; its proof is a-named-ask-main-did-not-select-runs-after-it. (b) flow's point 3 needs an asker-gone signal the